==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-lw-i}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁(y)-||to suckle}}. Cognate with Ancient Greek {{m|grc|θῆλυς}}.<ref>{{R:De Vaan 2008}}</ref> See also {{m|la|fēmina}}, {{m|la|fētus}}, {{m|la|fēcundus}}, {{m|la|fēnus}}, {{m|la|fīlius}}, {{m|la|fellō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|fēlīx}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-3rd-1E|fēlīx|fēlīcis|comp=fēlīcior|sup=fēlīcissimus}}

# [[happy]], [[lucky]], [[blessed]], [[fortunate]]
# [[fertile]], [[fruitful]], [[prosperous]]
# [[auspicious]], [[favorable]], of [[good]] [[omen]] or [[luck]]
# {{lb|la|religion|archaic}} of the [[noble]] [[fruit]]s offered to the [[deity|deities]]

